  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Statistics II: median and quartiles of ungrouped data</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core and Essential 3.1: Order a list and find the median and quartiles at positions (n + 1)/2, (n + 1)/4 and 3(n + 1)/4.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question B2 in Section B of Chapter 1 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: the quartile rule is changed to (n + 1) positions with interpolation, with a new Kenyan context and new data.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
